  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The damaged Immortal Gu House Thieves Den has one working ability: it uses theft path immortal materials as catalyst, instantly consumes the theft path dao marks in those materials, and steals dao marks from the outside world. The stolen marks attach to those materials, which end up filled with disorderly dao marks of every path and lose further value.",
      "chapters": [
        1865
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "house_thieves_den"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "General dao marks and attainment levels are covered on dao marks and attainment.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_dao_marks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Thieves Den’s killer move Steal Dao follows the same principle: theft path dao marks in the catalyst materials are consumed at once, outside dao marks are stolen, and the stolen marks must attach to those theft path immortal materials.",
      "chapters": [
        2133
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "steal-dao",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "move_steal_dao"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Thieving Heaven Demon Venerable expended his own theft path dao marks to refine gamble Gu. As an otherworldly demon he held otherworldly dao marks, and gamble Gu was refined from his otherworldly theft path dao marks, yielding random results that even Immortal Zombie Giant Sun’s luck could not interfere with.",
